 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Once upon time, in the shadow of an old oak tree, there was a fire. The fire was lit by the spirits who lived in the oak tree, and they told it at sunset when the moon was small and quiet. He wasn't a ghost, he was spirit, and he liked to tell stories around fire. He probably will, and that's part of the charm. He told the kids around the fire that when he told his story, they kept it going sure. Once, during a storm, the old tree fell on the house where the fire was, and the family had to sleep in the church down the hill. The spirit told the oldest kid to sit by the fire all night, keeping it going for his family.",
